---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
---

<BaseLayout title={`4D Product & Growth Decision Canvas — ${site.name}`} description="A printable one-page canvas connecting customer evidence, strategic choices, delivery scope, distribution, and success measures.">
  <header class="page-hero container no-print">
    <p class="eyebrow">Free working tool</p>
    <h1>The 4D Product & Growth <span class="accent">Decision Canvas.</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">Use it before a roadmap, launch, redesign, or campaign to expose where different functions are operating from different assumptions.</p>
    <div class="button-row"><button class="button" type="button" data-print>Print or save as PDF</button><a class="button button--ghost" href="/contact/">Apply it together</a></div>
  </header>
  <section class="canvas-wrap">
    <div class="canvas" aria-label="4D Product and Growth Decision Canvas">
      <header><div><span>HARKINGBADE / TOOL 01</span><h2>4D Decision Canvas</h2></div><div class="canvas-meta"><p>Initiative: ____________________</p><p>Date: ____________________</p><p>Owner: ____________________</p></div></header>
      <section class="prompt north"><span>North-star decision</span><h3>What consequential decision must this work enable?</h3><div class="write-lines"></div></section>
      <div class="canvas-grid">
        <section class="prompt"><span>01 / Discover</span><h3>What do we know?</h3><ul><li>Who is experiencing the problem?</li><li>What are they trying to change?</li><li>Which evidence is observed vs assumed?</li><li>What alternatives do they use now?</li></ul><div class="write-lines"></div></section>
        <section class="prompt"><span>02 / Define</span><h3>What choices are we making?</h3><ul><li>Target customer and moment</li><li>Problem and value proposition</li><li>Product or offer bet</li><li>What are we explicitly not doing?</li></ul><div class="write-lines"></div></section>
        <section class="prompt"><span>03 / Deliver</span><h3>What must become real?</h3><ul><li>Smallest experience that creates value</li><li>Message, product, and operational scope</li><li>Owner, dependencies, and constraints</li><li>Instrumentation required at launch</li></ul><div class="write-lines"></div></section>
        <section class="prompt"><span>04 / Drive</span><h3>How will we learn and grow?</h3><ul><li>Audience and distribution route</li><li>Activation or conversion moment</li><li>Leading and outcome measures</li><li>Decision rule after the first signal</li></ul><div class="write-lines"></div></section>
      </div>
      <section class="prompt south"><span>Evidence gate</span><h3>What must be true before we invest more?</h3><div class="write-lines"></div></section>
      <footer><span>harkingbade.com/resources/4d-decision-canvas</span><span>Share with attribution · Do not resell</span></footer>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section no-print">
    <div class="narrow prose"><h2>How to use it</h2><ol><li>Ask each function to complete the canvas independently before a planning meeting.</li><li>Compare the answers. Highlight conflicting customer, problem, promise, scope, and measure assumptions.</li><li>Resolve only the disagreements that change the decision or delivery scope.</li><li>Record unknowns as hypotheses with an owner and evidence deadline.</li><li>Set the evidence gate before work begins. Do not move the goalposts after seeing the result.</li></ol><div class="notice"><strong>Important</strong>The canvas is a decision aid, not proof. Customer claims still need customer evidence; growth claims still need measured behaviour.</div></div>
  </section>
  <script>document.querySelector('[data-print]')?.addEventListener('click', () => window.print());</script>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .canvas-wrap { padding: 2rem; overflow-x: auto; background: #d7d7d1; }
  .canvas { width: min(100%, 80rem); min-width: 68rem; margin: auto; padding: 1.5rem; border: 2px solid var(--ink); color: var(--ink); background: #fffdf7; box-shadow: var(--shadow); }
  .canvas > header { display: flex; padding-bottom: 1rem; justify-content: space-between; border-bottom: 3px solid var(--ink); }
  .canvas > header span, .prompt > span, .canvas footer { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: .65rem; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .canvas > header h2 { margin-top: .25rem; font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 2rem; font-weight: 900; letter-spacing: -.04em; }
  .canvas-meta { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: .7rem; line-height: 1.8; }
  .prompt { min-height: 19rem; padding: 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--ink); }
  .prompt > span { display: inline-block; padding: .2rem .45rem; color: var(--paper-2); background: var(--ink); }
  .prompt h3 { margin-block: .7rem; font-size: 1.25rem; }
  .prompt ul { padding-left: 1rem; font-size: .75rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .north, .south { min-height: 7rem; border-top: 0; }
  .canvas-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); }
  .canvas-grid .prompt + .prompt { border-left: 0; }
  .write-lines { margin-top: 1rem; height: 4rem; background: repeating-linear-gradient(transparent 0 1.3rem, #c5c5be 1.3rem calc(1.3rem + 1px)); }
  .north .write-lines, .south .write-lines { height: 1.5rem; }
  .canvas footer { display: flex; padding-top: .75rem; justify-content: space-between; }
  @media print {
    @page { size: landscape; margin: 8mm; }
    .no-print, :global(.site-header), :global(.site-footer) { display: none !important; }
    .canvas-wrap { padding: 0; background: #fff; }
    .canvas { width: 100%; min-width: 0; box-shadow: none; }
    .prompt { min-height: 0; }
  }
</style>
